WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.375
Step 1. Open Product Knowledge.

1.2
00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:07.243
Product Knowledge describes a product that the facility stocks or uses,

1.3
00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:13.503
such as a medication. In Settings, in the Inventory group, select Product Knowledge.

2.1
00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:15.617
Step 2. Open the category.

2.2
00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:21.066
Keep opening subcategories until you reach a category with no subcategories.

2.3
00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:24.721
Care shows Add Product Knowledge only there.

3.1
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:29.013
Step 3. Start the Product Knowledge. Select Add Product Knowledge,

3.2
00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:34.534
and Care opens the Create Product Knowledge form for the category that you opened.

4.1
00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.384
Step 4. Enter the basic information.

4.2
00:00:37.384 --> 00:00:40.851
Name, Slug, Category and Base Unit are required.

4.3
00:00:40.851 --> 00:00:47.058
Care fills in the slug from the name, and sets the status to Active by default.

5.1
00:00:47.058 --> 00:00:51.035
Step 5. Add alternative names. This step is optional.

5.2
00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:56.170
Select Add Name for each other name of the product, such as a trade name,

5.3
00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.428
and choose its Name Type.

6.1
00:00:58.428 --> 00:01:02.940
Step 6. Add storage guidelines. This step is also optional.

6.2
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.718
Select Add Guideline, then record how to store the product and how long it stays

6.3
00:01:08.718 --> 00:01:10.149
stable.

7.1
00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:13.899
Step 7. Complete or remove the product definition.

7.2
00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:17.539
While this section is open, Dosage Form is required.

7.3
00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:27.898
Select a Dosage Form and its routes, or select Remove Definition.

8.1
00:01:27.898 --> 00:01:31.661
Step 8. Create the Product Knowledge. Select Create.

8.2
00:01:31.661 --> 00:01:35.038
Care shows Product knowledge created successfully.

8.3
00:01:35.038 --> 00:01:41.009
If the status is Active, pickers offer it, for example when you create a product.
